# Replay payloads are DATA, not source, and must never be reformatted.
#
# `public/gallery/` is committed and deployed, and it is written minified by
# `build_replay.py --compact` — 2.3x smaller, and nobody reads a replay payload as a
# diff. Prettier reformatting one silently undoes that: measured, pretty-printing the
# three assets takes the gallery from 4.09 MB to 6.1 MB and over its budget.
#
# `src/engine/__fixtures__/` and the pipeline goldens are byte-compared by tests; a
# formatting pass would produce phantom diffs there for the same non-reason.
#
# This is a second line of defence, not the first: `app/src/data/galleryAssets.test.ts`
# fails if an asset arrives pretty-printed or the set exceeds 6 MB. The gate catches
# it; this stops it happening.
public/gallery/
public/data/
src/engine/__fixtures__/
dist/
coverage/
